      "url": "https://github.com/knowledgeislands/ki-agent-backpack/blob/ec0078018250b2ceb6f114ac0085a38e0f969a7c/skills/keystone/ki-agentic-ecosystems/knowledge/products/product.openclaw.md",
      "summaryHtml": "OpenClaw is a personal AI agent its user controls from the chat apps they already use, &quot;the AI that really does things&quot; (<a href=\"https://openclaw.ai\">S1</a>). The OpenClaw Foundation makes it, a US 501(c)(3) that &quot;employs the core team and signs releases&quot;; Peter Steinberger created it, and it was called Clawd and then Moltbot before OpenClaw (<a href=\"https://openclaw.ai\">S1</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw\">S2</a>, <a href=\"https://openclaw.ai/blog/introducing-openclaw\">S4</a>). A local Gateway is &quot;the local control plane for sessions, tools, events, and channel connections&quot;, with a CLI, a terminal interface, a browser Control UI and apps for desktop and mobile (<a href=\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw\">S2</a>). It runs its own agent and other makers' harnesses, so it is an <a href=\"https://github.com/knowledgeislands/ki-agent-backpack/blob/ec0078018250b2ceb6f114ac0085a38e0f969a7c/skills/keystone/ki-agentic-ecosystems/knowledge/industry/industry.agent-harness.md\">agent harness</a> and an <a href=\"https://github.com/knowledgeislands/ki-agent-backpack/blob/ec0078018250b2ceb6f114ac0085a38e0f969a7c/skills/keystone/ki-agentic-ecosystems/knowledge/industry/industry.agent-host.md\">agent host</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.openclaw.ai/concepts/agent-runtimes\">S13</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.openclaw.ai/cli/acp\">S14</a>). It is MIT open source: &quot;No subscription. No hosted tier. No token.&quot; (<a href=\"https://openclaw.ai\">S1</a>). The latest release seen is 2026.11.6, of 19 November 2026 (<a href=\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/releases\">S3</a>). It is a <a href=\"https://github.com/knowledgeislands/ki-agent-backpack/blob/ec0078018250b2ceb6f114ac0085a38e0f969a7c/skills/keystone/ki-agentic-ecosystems/knowledge/industry/industry.client.md\">client</a>.",
